# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Kept out of the repo intentionally (see CLAUDE.md)
internal-docs/
.claude/
.agents/

# hivemind build output and runtime state
/bin/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/uploads/

# node / frontend build output
node_modules/
web/dist/
docs/dist/
data/

# internal/web/dist holds the built frontend, go:embed'd into the binary.
# Keep a placeholder index.html tracked so the package compiles on a fresh
# checkout before `make ui` has run; ignore everything else generated there.
internal/web/dist/*
!internal/web/dist/index.html

